><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14b: yes there were practical reflections on the outcomes of the study</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="5" rect="595.260010,120.435928,779.260010,212.435928"
/></highlight
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20250616150151+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="21006a86-731d-4dd1-bae6-46417e58c23a" date="D:20250616150151+10'00'" name="fc3cff8d-1e5c-4142-a97b-739094162bca" icon="Comment" page="5" rect="44.541672,188.722824,68.541672,212.722824" subject="Sticky Note" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>At no timepoint was every coach able to rate every athlete&#xD;suggesting a “bandwidth” limit to the observational capacity of&#xD;a coach during the identification process. This indicates that&#xD;having a single coach evaluate multiple athletes is not an ideal&#xD;scenario, as coaches are unable to form a consistent opinion of&#xD;an athlete’s talent that they are comfortable with. This finding&#xD;supports previous research by </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#4C4C4C;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Roberts et al. (2020)</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>, who found&#xD;that coaches require time to get to know athletes before forming&#xD;a confident evaluation of the athlete’s future sporting potential. In&#xD;this study, although the coaches had 4 days in which to evaluate&#xD;the athletes, it appears that the number of athletes inhibited the&#xD;coaches’ capacity to survey the athletes in as much detail as they&#xD;would require to make confident judgments and decisions.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="5" rect="595.260010,120.722839,779.260010,212.722839"
/></text
></annots
